// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
; specs/turbobaby/locale_policy.t27 -- which languages this shop PUBLISHES, and what an
; unpublished one resolves to.
; Four facts are the subject: the two-locale set of DECISIONS.md D13, which of the two is
; primary, the single target every unpublished code falls to, and the measured gap between that
; published set and the variant set the code enumerates. Everything else below is evidence about
; those four -- the two resolvers, the two defaults, the key count and the gates that hold it --
; and not a fifth subject. It owns no wording, no key, no glyph and no number format.
; --
; WHY (measured 2026-09-20). The published set and the enumerated set are different sizes and
; nothing said so. src/locales.rs:119-121 supported_langs returns TWO codes, and that vector is
; what a customer is shown: it is the list the language picker is built from at
; src/bot/callbacks.rs:320-326 and src/bot/commands.rs:423-429, one button per element. But
; src/trios/core.rs:8-17 declares EIGHT Lang variants, src/trios/i18n.rs:2181-2192
; supported_languages returns all eight, and src/trios/i18n.rs:721-732 t() dispatches on all
; eight -- two to their own table (723, 724) and SIX to the English one (725-730, each arm
; carrying the comment Fallback to English). So six of the eight names this code can hold are
; labels with no table behind them, and the gap is exactly six because the two variants that
; have a table are the two the shop publishes. That coincidence is measured below, not assumed.
; --
; WHY THE GAP IS NOT HARMLESS (measured 2026-09-20). It is reachable and it is silent. The web
; client resolves a locale at src/trios/core.rs:197-213 pick_lang, whose first source is a URL
; parameter: lang=th parses through src/trios/core.rs:34-48 FromStr into Lang::Thai
; (src/trios/core.rs:106-107 witnesses exactly that), and the value survives the resolver as a
; live Lang: src/lib.rs:77 and src/lib.rs:81 hand it to src/ui/lang.rs:55-62 current_lang, whose
; readers pass it to src/trios/i18n.rs:721-732 t(), which answers out of the English table, and
; to src/ui/lang.rs:72-77 localized, which prefers the English column for any non-Russian
; language. The shipped consequence of an unpublished code on the web is therefore English text
; under an application state that says Thai. The bot half behaves differently and better:
; src/locales.rs:105-110 get_locale collapses an unpublished code before any lookup happens, so
; there is no distinct object left to carry the name. Two layers, two behaviours, one published
; set -- which is why the set needed an owner rather than a second opinion.
; --
; WHAT IS NOT SHIPPED, AND IS RECORDED ANYWAY (measured 2026-09-20). One step further would be a
; payload LABELLED with the unpublished code over English text. The repository contains the code
; for that and does not run it: src/trios/i18n.rs:1951 get_translations is the only writer of
; Translations.lang (src/trios/i18n.rs:2174-2176, from Lang::as_str), and its only caller in the
; whole tree is the unit test at src/trios/i18n.rs:2239-2240. Nothing under src/ui, src/api or
; src/bot calls it, no other site stamps a resolved code into output, and index.html:2 hard-codes
; the document language. So the mislabelled payload is a latent shape and not a customer-facing
; fact today. label_and_text_agree models the shape, MISLABELLED_PAYLOAD_IS_NOT_SHIPPED records
; that it is not reached, and neither one is allowed to stand in for the other.
; --
; WHERE THE ISSUE IS REFUTED. The survey that commissioned this file recorded that no key-parity
; gate exists. That is FALSE, and measurably so. src/trios/i18n.rs:2332 declares
; every_declared_key_has_a_russian_and_an_english_translation, which walks the declarations
; returned by declared_keys (src/trios/i18n.rs:2262-2283, parsing the file through include_str
; so the gate also builds for wasm32) and fails when either table is missing one. A SECOND gate,
; src/trios/i18n.rs:2374 every_translation_key_is_translated_in_ru_and_en, does the same walk
; through std::fs. Parity is gated twice. What the survey should have said is the thing the gate
; itself says at src/trios/i18n.rs:2326-2330: has_translation is get_ru_translation(key) != key,
; so a translation whose text equalled its own key would read as missing -- a false alarm, never
; a silent pass. That limitation is recorded below in the gate's own terms, and the gate's real
; blind spot is recorded separately: it walks DECLARED keys, so a literal handed to t() that was
; never declared is outside its reach, which src/trios/i18n.rs:2222-2226 demonstrates by
; asserting that an unknown key comes back as itself.
; --
; A SECOND CORRECTION, TO THE MEASUREMENT METHOD. The brief prescribed
; grep -c "pub const T_" src/trios/i18n.rs for the key count. That command returns 524 and five
; of those lines are not declarations: src/trios/i18n.rs:2256, 2363 and 2379 are prose, and 2265
; and 2383 are the two key parsers matching their own source text. The declaration count is 519,
; which is also what both gates find, and 519 is what is pinned below (declarations/grep: 523/528
; before the referral top list, 526/531 before R3's referral copy, 545/550 before 19 leftovers, 547/552
; before question I, all 2026-09-26; 552/557 before the list of 2026-09-25; same five lines).
; --
; WHAT THIS FILE NEVER DOES. It carries no translated string and no Cyrillic: L3 forbids
; Cyrillic in a spec, and turbobaby/pricing-honesty already set the precedent for the whole
; corpus by pinning the must-say obligation while leaving its Russian sentence to the locale
; layer. It owns two declarations that carry the precedent: MUST_SAY, which states the
; obligation in English, and RenderedRate, whose typed triple pins the shape and the amount and
; leaves the wording to the locale layer. Both were re-opened 2026-09-21 and both still mean
; what this sentence claims. They were cited by line until then, and the line numbers had
; already drifted: the first pointed one line past the sentence it meant. That precedent is
; named here as REUSES_PRICING_HONESTY_ID and applied to all 519 keys at once. It declares no key list --
; restating 519 identifiers would be the largest duplication in this repository, and it would be
; the fourth hand-maintained copy of a list that already has three. It publishes no third
; locale, and that prohibition is structural: the LENGTH of the published array, pinned by an
; invariant. It declares no currency glyph, separator, exponent or number format; those are
; fields of the market profile and REUSES_MARKET_PROFILE_ID names their owner. It states no
; market language fact either: what languages the MARKET speaks belongs to market_profile.t27,
; what the APPLICATION publishes belongs here, and the two agreeing today is a measurement below
; rather than an inheritance. No renter, handle, phone or note enters this file (D14).
; phi^2 + 1/phi^2 = 3 | TRINITY

module turbobaby-locale-policy;

pub const KIND : str = "contract";
pub const ID : str = "turbobaby/locale-policy";
pub const NAME : str = "TurboBaby published locale set";
pub const WORLD : str = "gHashTag/turbobaby-user-bot";
pub const DECISIONS : [2]str = ["D13", "D14"];
pub const MEASURED_AT : str = "2026-09-20";

; --- Ownership edges -----------------------------------------------------------------------
; The pinned compiler lowers a brace import to an empty UseDecl, so a cross-contract edge is a
; named ID plus a test that asserts the literal. market_profile.t27 owns the market language
; fact and every display convention; pricing_honesty.t27 owns the precedent that an obligation
; is pinned while its Russian wording is not.
pub const REUSES_MARKET_PROFILE_ID : str = "turbobaby/market";
pub const REUSES_PRICING_HONESTY_ID : str = "turbobaby/pricing-honesty";
pub const WORDING_RULE : str = "Pin the obligation, never the translation (L3). Applied here to every declared key at once: the COUNT is owned by this file, the text of each key is owned by the two tables in src/trios/i18n.rs.";

; --- The published set ---------------------------------------------------------------------
; src/locales.rs:119-121 supported_langs returns two codes, and that vector is the
; customer-visible list: src/bot/callbacks.rs:320-326 and src/bot/commands.rs:423-429 each build
; one picker button per element. Its LENGTH is the prohibition on a third locale.
pub const PUBLISHED_LOCALE_COUNT : u8 = 2;
pub const PUBLISHED_LOCALES : [2]str = ["ru", "en"];
pub const PUBLISHED_SET_SOURCE : str = "src/locales.rs:119-121 supported_langs";
pub const PUBLISHED_SET_REACHES_THE_CUSTOMER_AT : str = "src/bot/callbacks.rs:320-326 and src/bot/commands.rs:423-429, one picker button per element";
; DECISIONS.md:181-184 D13: two locales, ru and en, no Thai. The reason it states is a STAFFING
; fact and not a demand estimate -- clients are handled only by Russian-speaking managers and
; the Thai team does not deal with clients. Russian is primary.
pub const PRIMARY_LOCALE : str = "ru";
pub const PRIMARY_LOCALE_DECISION : str = "DECISIONS.md:181-184 D13";
; The single fallback target. It is itself a member of the published set, and that membership is
; what makes resolution total rather than merely defined.
pub const FALLBACK_LOCALE : str = "en";
; THE ONE VALUE THIS FILE SHARES WITH ANOTHER CONTRACT, named here so it is found by its author
; before it is found by a reviewer. turbobaby/market owns TH_LANGUAGES, and it carries the same
; two codes. It is a DIFFERENT measurement with a different source: that one is a field of the
; deployment's market profile -- what the MARKET speaks -- and this one is read off
; src/locales.rs:119-121, what the APPLICATION publishes. They coincide today because this shop
; publishes its own market's languages, and nothing forces that: a second market profile would
; carry other codes while this set stayed at two, and a shop may publish a locale its market
; does not speak. Neither file reads the other, and this one would not change if that one did.
; Named by owner ID and declaration name, not by line. This citation used to read
; "specs/turbobaby/market_profile.t27:109 TH_LANGUAGES" and it went stale on 2026-09-21 while
; being read: an edit to that file's header moved TH_LANGUAGES from line 109 to line 151, and
; line 109 is now blank. A declaration name survives an edit to its own file; a line number does
; not, and it fails silently and authoritatively.
pub const MARKET_LANGUAGE_FIELD : str = "turbobaby/market TH_LANGUAGES";
pub const PUBLISHED_SET_IS_INHERITED_FROM_THE_MARKET : bool = false;
pub const SETS_COINCIDE_TODAY : bool = true;

; --- The two resolvers ---------------------------------------------------------------------
; Bot half: src/locales.rs:105-110 get_locale matches ru and sends everything else to en()
; through the bare catch-all arm at src/locales.rs:108. An unpublished code never becomes a
; distinct Locale object, so there is nothing left to mislabel.
pub const BOT_RESOLVER : str = "src/locales.rs:105-110 get_locale";
pub const BOT_RESOLVER_HAS_CATCH_ALL_ARM : bool = true;
pub const BOT_RESOLVER_COLLAPSES_UNPUBLISHED : bool = true;
; Web half: src/trios/core.rs:197-213 pick_lang returns a Lang, and an unpublished variant
; survives as a value. Live call sites are src/lib.rs:77 and src/lib.rs:81, which park the
; resolved variant in src/ui/lang.rs:55-62 current_lang; from there t() answers out of the
; English table and localized prefers the English column. That much is shipped.
pub const WEB_RESOLVER : str = "src/trios/core.rs:197-213 pick_lang";
pub const WEB_RESOLVER_KEEPS_UNPUBLISHED_VARIANT : bool = true;
pub const WEB_RESOLVER_LIVE_CALL_SITES : str = "src/lib.rs:77 and src/lib.rs:81, into src/ui/lang.rs:55-62 current_lang";
pub const WEB_UNPUBLISHED_RENDERS_ENGLISH_AT : str = "src/trios/i18n.rs:721-732 t() and src/ui/lang.rs:72-77 localized";
; THE STEP THAT IS WRITTEN AND NOT RUN, kept apart from the step that ships. A payload labelled
; with the unpublished code over English text needs src/trios/i18n.rs:1951 get_translations, the
; only writer of Translations.lang (src/trios/i18n.rs:2174-2176, from Lang::as_str). Its only
; caller in the tree is the unit test at src/trios/i18n.rs:2239-2240; nothing under src/ui,
; src/api or src/bot calls it, no other site stamps a resolved code into output, and
; index.html:2 hard-codes the document language. The shape exists and is not reached.
pub const WEB_LABEL_SITE : str = "src/trios/i18n.rs:1951 get_translations, stamping Translations.lang at src/trios/i18n.rs:2174-2176";
pub const MISLABELLED_PAYLOAD_IS_NOT_SHIPPED : bool = true;
pub const MISLABELLED_PAYLOAD_NOTE : str = "get_translations has no production caller: the only one in the tree is the test at src/trios/i18n.rs:2239-2240. The mislabelled payload is a latent shape in the code, never a measured customer fact. It would become one the day a production caller appears, and this contract would have to be re-measured then.";
; src/trios/core.rs:212, the last line of pick_lang, defaults to Lang::Russian, which agrees
; with D13. migrations/001_initial.sql:4 defaults the stored column to en, which does not. Both
; are measured; neither is corrected here, because a default belongs to the surface that holds
; it and this file only records that the two disagree.
pub const WEB_DEFAULT_LOCALE : str = "ru";
pub const STORAGE_DEFAULT_LOCALE : str = "en";
pub const DEFAULTS_AGREE : bool = false;
pub const STORAGE_COLUMN : str = "migrations/001_initial.sql:4 user_languages.language VARCHAR(10) NOT NULL DEFAULT en";
; Measured by searching every .sql file under migrations/ for a CHECK or a constraint naming
; that column: there is none. The search is recursive and the count says so -- 89 files sit at
; the top level and one more in migrations/wip, and a top-level-only count would have been 89
; while claiming to have looked everywhere. src/db/mod.rs:904-927 set_user_lang writes the code
; it is handed after a length truncation (src/db/mod.rs:907, to 50 characters), with no
; membership test. So the store admits a code the shop does not publish, and the read path
; resolves it exactly like any other unpublished code.
pub const MIGRATION_FILES_SEARCHED : u8 = 90;
pub const STORAGE_CONSTRAINS_THE_PUBLISHED_SET : bool = false;
; WHOSE COUNT THIS IS. turbobaby/pricing-honesty raised the same figure first, in a declaration
; of the same name, for a different search over the same directory. Two contracts declaring one
; measurement with no edge between them is the drift D15 exists to remove, so the count is OWNED
; there and carried HERE as a named copy. The declaration above stays -- this file's own tests
; read it, and a contract that cannot check its own sentence is a claim -- but it is a copy, and
; the edge below says so and says whose. Re-measured 2026-09-21 and unchanged: a recursive
; search of migrations/ for .sql files returns 87, of which 86 sit at the top level and one in
; migrations/wip. The only non-.sql file under migrations/ is migrations/wip/README.md, which is
; why counting every file gives 88 and is the wrong arithmetic for this claim.
; CORRECTED 2026-09-24, with the owner's figure: 88 recursive, 87 at the top level, 89 counting
; every file. migrations/087_delivery_zones_phuket.sql arrived (turbobaby/delivery-terms); it holds
; no CHECK and no constraint on a language column, so the search still finds none. The two
; src/db/mod.rs citations above moved four lines when that file joined MIGRATIONS (892-915 and 895
; before). The 2026-09-21 count is kept under its own name.
; CORRECTED 2026-09-24, later the same day: 89 recursive, 88 at the top level, 90 counting every
; file. migrations/088_unpublish_events.sql arrived (turbobaby/events-booking, the owner's
; rental-only ruling); it holds no CHECK and no constraint on a language column, so the search
; still finds none. The two src/db/mod.rs citations above moved four more lines when it joined
; MIGRATIONS (896-919 and 899 between the two changes). The count between them is kept under
; _BEFORE_088; the next paragraph's figures are the census as it stood before 088.
; CORRECTED 2026-09-24, the same day: the owner named here was the wrong one. turbobaby/pricing-honesty called
; the count its own, and so did turbobaby/schema-provenance, whose subject is the migration tree and
; which declares the census as SQL_FILES_RECURSIVE 88 (with SQL_FILES_TOP_LEVEL 87 and WIP_SQL_FILES
; 1) and lists this file among its sibling copies. The two owners were resolved that day in favour
; of schema-provenance, and pricing-honesty now carries its figure as a copy too. So this copy names
; the census owner directly, by ID and declaration, instead of a file that is itself a copy. This
; file's own search is unchanged by the re-pointing; the edge as first written is kept below under
; _BEFORE_ names.
pub const MIGRATION_COUNT_OWNER_ID : str = "turbobaby/schema-provenance";
pub const MIGRATION_COUNT_OWNER_DECL : str = "SQL_FILES_RECURSIVE";
pub const MIGRATION_COUNT_OWNER_ID_BEFORE_2026_09_24 : str = "turbobaby/pricing-honesty";
pub const MIGRATION_COUNT_OWNER_DECL_BEFORE_2026_09_24 : str = "MIGRATION_FILES_SEARCHED";
pub const MIGRATION_COUNT_IS_A_COPY : bool = true;
pub const MIGRATION_COUNT_REMEASURED_AT : str = "2026-09-24";
pub const MIGRATION_COUNT_OWNER_REPOINTED_AT : str = "2026-09-24";
; CORRECTED 2026-09-26: 90 recursive, 89 at the top level. migrations/089_referral_credit.sql
; arrived (turbobaby/referral-credit, the owner's R3 answer); it holds no CHECK and no constraint on
; a language column, so the search still finds none. The two src/db/mod.rs citations above moved
; four more lines when it joined MIGRATIONS (900-923 and 903 before). The count before it is kept
; under _BEFORE_089.
pub const MIGRATION_FILES_SEARCHED_BEFORE_087 : u8 = 87;
pub const MIGRATION_FILES_SEARCHED_BEFORE_088 : u8 = 88;
pub const MIGRATION_FILES_SEARCHED_BEFORE_089 : u8 = 89;

; --- The enumerated variant set, and the gap -------------------------------------------------
; src/trios/core.rs:8-17 enum Lang: Russian, English, Thai, Chinese, Hebrew, German, French,
; Spanish. src/trios/i18n.rs:721-732 t() dispatches on all eight: 723 and 724 reach their own
; table, 725 through 730 reach the English one.
pub const ENUMERATED_VARIANT_COUNT : u8 = 8;
pub const ENUMERATED_VARIANT_SOURCE : str = "src/trios/core.rs:8-17 enum Lang; src/trios/i18n.rs:721-732 t()";
pub const VARIANTS_WITH_OWN_TABLE : u8 = 2;
pub const VARIANTS_FALLING_THROUGH_TO_ENGLISH : u8 = 6;

; --- The key tables ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; The COUNT, never the keys. 565 declarations in src/trios/i18n.rs, every literal distinct. Two
; hand-maintained match blocks translate them: get_ru_translation at src/trios/i18n.rs:735 and
; get_en_translation at src/trios/i18n.rs:1335.
; Re-measured 2026-09-25, when T_ORDER_DETAIL_CANCEL_REFUSED was declared for the client-errors
; contract's refused-cancellation sentence: one declaration and one arm per table, so both counts
; rose by one (565 to 566, 570 to 571), and every src/trios/i18n.rs line this file cites was
; re-read at its new address and carries the same claim.
; CORRECTED 2026-09-25: 552, not 565. The owner's ruling of that day (#12, nothing cannabis-related
; anywhere) deleted fourteen keys outright and added none; turbobaby/legacy-retirement records what
; they were (CANNABIS_RULING_I18N_KEYS_DELETED). Each deleted line was replaced one-for-one by a
; comment line, so that deletion moved no src/trios/i18n.rs line cited in this file, and the naive
; grep below falls by the same fourteen, 571 to 557, over the same five non-declaration lines. The
; two changes landed together on 2026-09-25 (565 + 1 - 14 = 552; 570 + 1 - 14 = 557, both
; re-measured on the merged file, and the file header now says so). The 565 and 570 of the
; 2026-09-20 reading are kept below under _BEFORE_2026_09_25 names.
; CORRECTED 2026-09-25, later the same day: 551, not 552. The owner's second numbered list of that
; day answered its item 5 "probably" to removing the bike detail screen's all-taken line, and that
; line's key, bike.units.empty, was deleted outright the way the fourteen were: its declaration and
; both of its arms each became a comment line, so no src/trios/i18n.rs line cited in this file
; moved, and the naive grep falls by the same one, 557 to 556, over the same five non-declaration
; lines. turbobaby/availability records what the key said and why it went (UNITS_EMPTY_KEY); the
; count is this file's, and the arithmetic in the key-count test below now subtracts both deletions.
; CORRECTED AGAIN 2026-09-25: 547, not 552. The owner removed the checkout's 20+ box for now the
; same day (answer 1 of a second numbered list), and the five keys the box used -- its label, its
; notice, the trust block's age line, the button's age blocker and the sentence for a body code
; the server never sent -- were deleted the way #12 deleted its fourteen: each line one-for-one
; by a comment line, so no src/trios/i18n.rs line cited in this file moved, and none added.
; turbobaby/checkout-contact records what they were (AGE_GATE_I18N_KEYS_DELETED_NAMES). The naive
; grep falls by the same five, 557 to 552, over the same five non-declaration lines
; (565 + 1 - 14 - 5 = 547; 570 + 1 - 14 - 5 = 552, both re-measured on the changed file).
; MERGED 2026-09-26: 546. The two corrections above were each measured on a branch that did not
; hold the other; on the integration branch both deletions are in the file, and the two
; paragraphs' 551 and 547 each still count one of them in. Re-measured on the merged file:
; 565 + 1 - 14 - 1 - 5 = 546 declarations; 570 + 1 - 14 - 1 - 5 = 551 for the naive grep, over
; the same five non-declaration lines, which did not move.
; CORRECTED 2026-09-25 again: 553, not 552. The owner's answer 3 of that day (the previous shop's
; stored content out of customers' sight) declared one key, T_ORDER_LINE_PREVIOUS_CATALOGUE, the
; neutral name a line of the old catalogue is shown under, with one arm per table; the naive grep
; rose with it, 557 to 558, over the same five non-declaration lines. The three lines were written
; over a blank line and two section comments, so no src/trios/i18n.rs line cited in this file
; moved. turbobaby/order-presentation owns the name (RETIRED_LINE_NAME_KEY) and records it.
; MERGED AGAIN 2026-09-26: 547. Answer 3's paragraph, too, was measured without the other two
; answers' deletions. Re-measured on the merged file: 565 + 2 - 14 - 1 - 5 = 547 declarations;
; 570 + 2 - 14 - 1 - 5 = 552 for the naive grep, over the same five non-declaration lines.
; CORRECTED 2026-09-26: 545, not 547. The owner answered question I that day (allow booking; a
; manager confirms availability), and the Book control's two reasons that read the seeded unit
; count went with it: bike.book.blocked.no_units and bike.book.blocked.unknown_availability were
; deleted outright, each declaration and each arm one-for-one by a comment line, so no
; src/trios/i18n.rs line cited in this file moved, and none was added. turbobaby/availability
; records what they were and why they went (NO_UNITS_BOOK_REASON_KEY,
; UNKNOWN_AVAILABILITY_BOOK_REASON_KEY). Re-measured on the changed file:
; 565 + 2 - 14 - 1 - 5 - 2 = 545 declarations; 570 + 2 - 14 - 1 - 5 - 2 = 550 for the naive grep,
; over the same five non-declaration lines.
; CORRECTED AGAIN 2026-09-26: 526, not 545. Nineteen keys of cannabis-era copy that the bundle still
; carried, although no mounted screen printed it, were deleted outright the same day under the
; owner's rulings of 2026-09-25 (#12 and answer 3): the garden's bonus label, two paraphernalia
; categories, the strain card's lab-certificate link and fifteen keys of the unmounted shop game's
; farm. Each declaration, each arm, and each of the thirteen rows the second parity gate's own list
; held, one-for-one by a comment line, so no src/trios/i18n.rs line cited in this file moved, and
; none was added. turbobaby/legacy-retirement records what they were (LEFTOVERS_2026_09_26_*).
; Re-measured on the changed file: 565 + 2 - 14 - 1 - 5 - 2 - 19 = 526 declarations;
; 570 + 2 - 14 - 1 - 5 - 2 - 19 = 531 for the naive grep, over the same five non-declaration lines.
; CORRECTED ONCE MORE 2026-09-26: 523, not 526. The owner answered R3 that day (the referral
; programme: 10% of every rental an invited friend completes, spent on a rental or paid out by a
; manager; the referral points stop). The referral screens' copy followed, and every edit replaced
; one line of src/trios/i18n.rs with one line, so no line cited in this file moved:
;   * SEVEN keys retired, each promising points, a ladder or an amount per friend that the shop no
;     longer credits: the milestone ladder's title, progress and rung, the fourth stat card's
;     label, the friend-facing share text, the empty friends panel's sentence and the profile's
;     amount per friend. Each declaration and each arm became a comment line naming the key;
;   * FOUR keys declared on four of those lines, the operator's wording under R3: the referral
;     balance, the hold against a rental, the payout request and its confirmation.
;   * The rule sentence kept its key and changed its text; the count does not see it.
; Which keys they are is not this file's (it carries no key): turbobaby/referral-credit owns the
; copy (its COPY_KEYS), and the unit test named by KEYS_DELETED_2026_09_26_R3_WITNESS holds the
; seven absent from the declarations and from both tables. Re-measured on the changed file:
; 526 + 4 - 7 = 523 declarations; 531 + 4 - 7 = 528 for the naive grep, over the same five
; non-declaration lines, which did not move. The 526 and 531 are kept under _BEFORE_2026_09_26_R3.
; CORRECTED AGAIN 2026-09-26: 519, not 523. The owner answered the same day, of the referral page's
; top-referrers list and the public address it read, "remove the top and close the address"
; (turbobaby/referral-program, OWNER_TOP_LIST_ANSWER_*). The list left the page, and the four keys
; only it used -- its title, its empty state, the masked id and the row's earnings line -- were
; deleted outright, each declaration and each arm one-for-one by a comment line, so no
; src/trios/i18n.rs line cited in this file moved, and none was added. turbobaby/referral-program
; names them (TOP_LIST_KEYS_RETIRED) and the unit test named by KEYS_DELETED_2026_09_26_TOP_LIST_WITNESS
; holds them absent from the declarations and from both tables. Re-measured on the changed file:
; 523 - 4 = 519 declarations; 528 - 4 = 524 for the naive grep, over the same five non-declaration
; lines. The 523 and 528 are kept under _BEFORE_THE_TOP_LIST_ANSWER.
pub const TRANSLATION_KEY_COUNT : u16 = 519;
